[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-019-input-validation-pattern.md#approach-3-output-encoding-for-xss-prevention]

### Approach 3: Output Encoding for XSS Prevention

**Overview:** Apply context-appropriate encoding to all user-controlled data before including in HTML, JavaScript, JSON, or URL responses.

**Implementation:**

```csharp
// ASP.NET Core Razor Pages - Automatic HTML Encoding
@model ProviderProfileModel

<div class="provider-profile">
    <!-- Razor automatically HTML-encodes model properties -->
    <h1>@Model.Provider.Name</h1>  <!-- Safe: <script> rendered as &lt;script&gt; -->
    <p>Specialty: @Model.Provider.Specialty</p>

    <!-- Explicit encoding for JavaScript context -->
    <script>
        var providerData = {
            name: '@Html.JavaScriptEncode(Model.Provider.Name)',
            npi: '@Model.Provider.Npi'
        };
    </script>

    <!-- URL encoding for query parameters -->
    <a href="/search?name=@Uri.EscapeDataString(Model.Provider.Name)">Search Similar</a>
</div>
```

**Node.js Express with Template Engine:**
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const escapeHtml = require('escape-html');

app.get('/providers/:npi', async (req, res) => {
    const provider = await db.getProvider(req.params.npi);

    // HTML encoding prevents XSS
    const html = `
        <h1>Provider Profile</h1>
        <div class="provider-name">${escapeHtml(provider.name)}</div>
        <div class="specialty">${escapeHtml(provider.specialty)}</div>
    `;

    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/html; charset=utf-8');
    res.setHeader('X-Content-Type-Options', 'nosniff');  // Prevent MIME sniffing
    res.send(html);
});

// JSON API responses - use res.json() for automatic encoding
app.get('/api/providers/:npi', async (req, res) => {
    const provider = await db.getProvider(req.params.npi);
    res.json(provider);  // Express automatically sanitizes JSON
});
```

**Content Security Policy Headers:**
```csharp
// Add CSP header to all responses
app.Use(async (context, next) =>
{
    context.Response.Headers.Add("Content-Security-Policy",
        "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'");
    context.Response.Headers.Add("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff");
    context.Response.Headers.Add("X-Frame-Options", "DENY");
    context.Response.Headers.Add("X-XSS-Protection", "1; mode=block");

    await next();
});
```

