[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-019-input-validation-pattern.md#preventing-proto-injection-at-the-body-parser-level]

##### Preventing __proto__ Injection at the Body Parser Level

Even before schema validation runs, configure Express's JSON body parser to strip `__proto__` and `constructor` keys from parsed objects:

```typescript
import express from 'express';

app.use(
  express.json({
    limit: '1mb',
    reviver: (key: string, value: unknown) => {
      // Strip prototype pollution vectors before the parsed object reaches any code
      if (key === '__proto__' || key === 'constructor' || key === 'prototype') {
        return undefined;
      }
      return value;
    },
  }),
);
```

This provides defense-in-depth: the body parser reviver removes pollution vectors, and `.strict()` on the zod schema provides a second layer of rejection.

