[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-019-input-validation-pattern.md#joi-alternative]

#### joi Alternative

For services that use `joi`, configure the schema to fail on unknown keys (equivalent to zod's `.strict()`):

```typescript
import Joi from 'joi';

const createMemberSchema = Joi.object({
  memberId: Joi.string().uuid().required(),
  dateOfBirth: Joi.string()
    .pattern(/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/)
    .required(),
  planCode: Joi.string().alphanum().min(1).max(20).required(),
  stateCode: Joi.string()
    .pattern(/^[A-Z]{2}$/)
    .length(2)
    .required(),
}).options({
  allowUnknown: false,  // Reject unknown keys — prevents prototype pollution pass-through
  stripUnknown: false,  // Never silently strip; always error on unexpected keys
});
```
